Usage: cygpath [OPTION] NAME...

Convert path names between Windows and Unix formats.
Convert path names between Windows and Unix/Cygwin formats.
Default is to convert Windows paths to Unix paths.

OPTIONS:
  -u, --unix           print Unix form of NAME
  -w, --windows        print Windows form of NAME
  -m, --mixed          print Windows form, with regular slashes
  -p, --path           NAME is a PATH list
  -t, --type ARG       print TYPE form: dos, mixed, unix, or windows
  -d, --dos            print DOS short form of NAMEs
  -a, --absolute       output absolute path [accepted, partial lexical support]
  -i, --ignore         ignore missing or empty arguments
  -f, --file ARG       read input paths from FILE
  -o, --option         read options from FILE as well [accepted, not
                       implemented]
  -l, --long-name      print Windows long form
  -s, --short-name     print DOS short form
  -U, --proc-cygdrive  emit /proc/cygdrive paths
  -C, --codepage ARG   print Windows path in codepage CP
  -M, --mode           report file text/binary mode
  -A, --allusers       use All Users for special folders
  -D, --desktop        output Desktop directory
  -H, --homeroot       output Profiles directory
  -O, --mydocs         output My Documents directory
  -P, --smprograms     output Start Menu Programs directory
  -S, --sysdir         output system directory
  -W, --windir         output Windows directory
  -F, --folder ARG     output special folder ID [not implemented]
      --help           display this help and exit
  -V, --version        output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
